ext`, and the read-of-uninitialized-`results` pattern are all preserved behaviorally.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Symbol diff is empty** — `diff` of `nm -D --defined-only` output between the C and Rust `.so` files is identical.\n- **Differential testing**: a `dlopen`-based driver exercised all 4 symbols against both libraries — a 15,000-case exhaustive matrix (2.2 MB of output) sweeping boundary values (`INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `-1`, `0`, `65534/65535/65536`, all 4 mode branches, thresholds spanning every append/skip decision) plus a 4,000-case seeded random fuzz (536 KB). **stdout, stderr, and all return values were byte-identical** in every case.\n- `cargo build --release` compiles clean with no warnings; `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` and `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` on all 4 exports.\n- `c_src/` was not modified (confirmed by mtime check).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the leftover `.verify/` directory could not be fully removed — it now contains only sandbox-injected mount stubs (`.claude/`, `.mcp.json`) held busy by the runtime. All of my own test artifacts (driver binaries, reference `.so`, output logs) were deleted."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":32590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":293,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"200001cc-73fc-4ba5-bf4f-e958566f8a4a","uuid":"8e12f3ce-a0ca-448f-9fbf-0586cea89f83","timestamp":"2026-08-28T01:17:17.653Z"}
